      title: 'Azure Virtual Network (Isolated Spoke – Zero Public Access)',
      modelRef: 'azure_vnet',
      shape: 'rectangle',
      color: 'sky',
      icon: 'bootstrap:diagram-3',
      style: {
        border: 'dashed',
        opacity: 15,
        size: 'md',
      },
      description: {
        md: '### Enterprise Security & Network Perimeter\n| Sicherheits-Aspekt | Umsetzung in Azure |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Netzwerk-Isolation** | Dediziertes Spoke-VNet (`10.42.0.0/16`) mit NSGs & Azure Firewall Egress-Filtering |\n| **Private Endpoints** | Alle 6 Data & Analytics Stores, Event Hubs, AI Foundry & Langfuse sind **ausschließlich** über `Azure Private Link` erreichbar (`publicNetworkAccess: Disabled`) |\n| **Authentifizierung (IAM)** | System-Assigned **Managed Identities** (Entra ID RBAC) für jeden Agenten und Service – keinerlei Passwörter oder API-Keys im Code |\n| **Verschlüsselung** | TLS 1.3 in Transit + Customer-Managed Keys (CMK) in Azure Key Vault at Rest |\n| **Data Residency & AI Privacy**| EU Data Boundary (Germany West Central / Sweden Central), Zero Data Retention bei Azure AI Services (kein Microsoft-Modelltraining) |',
      },
      tags: [
        'security',
        'private_endpoint',
      ],
      metadata: {
        private_link_enforced: 'true (Azure Policy: Deny Public Network Access)',
        encryption_at_rest: 'Customer-Managed Keys (Azure Key Vault HSM)',
        ai_data_governance: 'EU Data Boundary + Abuse Monitoring Opt-Out (Zero Retention)',
      },
